Description: Principal component analysis is a bidirectional method, as the sign
    of a principal direction carries no meaning. This package provides one-sided
    (directional) principal component analysis, in which each direction is
    considered separately. A linear version is based on positive-part
    projections, and a nonlinear version is based on the empirical
    center-outward quantile function of Hallin et al. (2021)
    <doi:10.1214/20-AOS1996>, with principal curves and curvilinear projections.
    For comparison, the independent nonlinear component analysis of Gunsilius and
    Schennach (2023) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2021.1990768> is also included.
